  <article class="about-page shell">

    <header class="about-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Fate Apothecary</p>
      <h1>Food, herbs, growing, and a little intuition.</h1>

      <p class="about-lede">
        Fate Apothecary started in 2023 with a deep dive into herbalism and a
        growing curiosity about all the ways we can take better care of ourselves.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-copy">

      <p>
        <strong>Somewhere along the way, we realized that conversation was much bigger than herbs.</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        It’s also the food we make. What we grow. What we keep in the pantry.
        The little things we learn and pass along to friends.
      </p>

      <p>So Fate has evolved.</p>

      <p>
        Today, it’s our growing collection of recipes, herbs, garden notes,
        kitchen knowledge, and practical ways to be a little more intentional
        about what goes into—and comes out of—our homes.
      </p>

      <p>
        We’re <strong>Beth and Matt</strong>, a husband-and-wife team in Fate,
        Texas. Beth is the gardener, herbalism nerd, and driving force behind
        Fate Apothecary, but the kitchen has always been a shared space. After
        23 years together, Matt has picked up plenty of Beth’s cooking habits
        and now handles much of the meat and grilling. Most of what we share
        here comes from the way we actually cook at home: together, by instinct,
        and with a lot of trust in our own taste buds.
      </p>

      <p>
        Around here, we cook with our hearts, occasionally let our ancestors
        decide when we’ve added enough seasoning, and firmly believe taking care
        of yourself doesn’t have to be complicated or perfect.
      </p>

      <p>
        We’re not trying to tell you how to live your life.
        <strong>We’re just sharing what we actually make, grow, use, learn, and love</strong>
        —hopefully in a way that makes something a little easier for you too.
      </p>

    </div>

    <aside class="about-note">
      <p class="eyebrow">A quick but important note</p>

      <p>
        We’re not medical professionals, and Fate Apothecary isn’t a substitute
        for medical care. Information about herbs, food, and wellness is shared
        for educational purposes. Herbs can interact with medications, health
        conditions, pregnancy, and each other, so please research what’s
        appropriate for you and talk with a qualified healthcare professional
        when needed.
      </p>
    </aside>

  </article>
